<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Fact check: Viral videos falsely linked to Riyadh airport attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe9d65bcca9c5ea23c10632eba6840d14bbd14ff6459f2d10cbb143896319a14</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037--a62cb3e36a4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many videos claiming to show an attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport have gone viral online. DW Fact check analyzes some of the most-shared footage and finds evidence it was created using AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Labor Minister's resignation puts a spotlight on cracks within the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3060fa754ae079aa391d4bdd03e0956737b4fe7f6c3fdbf8feb7af6e625e0437</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823--1507ba6fa4a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the sudden resignation of Bärbel Bas as Labor Minister and co-chair of the Social Democratic Party, accusations are flying in Chancellor Merz's coalition government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz says Trump's Russia diesel deal 'out of question' for Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d578dcd67b06f53f3480a27cb089a5bfbce7a3186e4387ab4ab4e2e833786061</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-says-trump-s-russia-diesel-deal-out-of-question-for-europe/live-79636427--1a9438e4fa1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-says-trump-s-russia-diesel-deal-out-of-question-for-europe/live-79636427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has said that Donald Trump's diesel deal with Russia would be "out of the question" for Germany and the EU. Meanwhile, the ruling coalition has been rocked by a major resignation. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US federal agents search home of Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8741766ece22ffc7fcb521122d8ce08da7c284d5887bc6a3a2ac436c124ef5b0</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-federal-agents-search-home-of-trump-critic-ilhan-omar/a-79643360--b11b8361cb7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-federal-agents-search-home-of-trump-critic-ilhan-omar/a-79643360?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Justice Department officials said the Washington residence of Democratic Congresswoman Ilhan Omar, an outspoken opponent of President Trump, was raided as "part of an ongoing federal investigation."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope lung nodule: Could it be cancer?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b2b6c4722d9ab777226e5bbee65b5a885916cbf0eaafbcd053bf6b1a1ff4b63</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503--9cf198017761.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The case of Pope Leo shows how small lung nodules are often found during routine health checks. Quick treatment is generally advised before nodules can grow to become larger life-threatening masses.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Starlink India launch: Why Elon Musk is still waiting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:280b401676ac697dc1657653276f4ec6853e0c9a2e09f2815be73555d92d013d</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043--4f745799dbba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite securing key approvals, the Starlink satellite internet service remains in regulatory limbo, raising questions about security clearances, competition and India’s investment climate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can South Korea and Ukraine resolve their diplomatic spat over North Korean POWs?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e0a30025c83f94430fb7ed1a1db1e4e039e527f7d63a77a531f032caa11e108</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-south-korea-and-ukraine-resolve-their-diplomatic-spat-over-north-korean-pows/a-79641352--b03ac996f9c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-south-korea-and-ukraine-resolve-their-diplomatic-spat-over-north-korean-pows/a-79641352?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul and Kyiv are trading accusations after the transfer of two North Korean POWs to South Korea. The South insists the move was to be kept secret as it seeks to avoid antagonizing Pyongyang.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus closer than ever to joining Schengen but political hurdles relating to the Green Line and British Sovereign Base Areas remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ad384eb99bc4781ea8f30bd2178d05d94522bd5de4bdce94d29804e5d78ab75</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-closer-than-ever-to-joining-schengen-but-political-hurdles-relating-to-the-green-line-and-bri/a-79641488--9447b5849bd1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-closer-than-ever-to-joining-schengen-but-political-hurdles-relating-to-the-green-line-and-british-sovereign-base-areas-remain/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Russia launched strikes hours after Donald Trump announced an 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:144df8f88dfc548162bf981615dae8a5fd2d2d4c2c178445a9ebfbee1b023618</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T11:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-russia-launched-strikes-hours-after-donald-trump-announced-an-energy-ceasefire/a-79640911--e71f7886c231.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-russia-launched-strikes-hours-after-donald-trump-announced-an-energy-ceasefire/a-79640911?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Less than 24 hours after Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire," Ukraine reported Russian strikes on the northeastern city of Kharkiv. The Kremlin says it would only consider a one-day ceasefire for an election.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Wadephul calls new EU sanctions 'unprecedented' blow to Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36f14cb99f5eaf3925e63b845da553be49739b2f344f86eb0bdbc06ea181a72d</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-calls-new-eu-sanctions-unprecedented-blow-to-russia/a-79638017--5ed7d4a3c799.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-calls-new-eu-sanctions-unprecedented-blow-to-russia/a-79638017?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union has approved its largest-ever sanctions package against Moscow, targeting more than 1,000 entities tied to the military-industrial complex. The move took place in an EU foreign ministers' meeting.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia: Deadly Houthi strikes on Riyadh airport fuel fears of wider Middle East conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6625b6bcf011fc8c95c8ceff7e4a466988256361a19486f03ca9aeb8d6bb1516</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-deadly-houthi-strikes-on-riyadh-airport-fuel-fears-of-wider-middle-east-conflict/live-79639277--e5c36dea696a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-deadly-houthi-strikes-on-riyadh-airport-fuel-fears-of-wider-middle-east-conflict/live-79639277?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Deadly Houthi attacks on Saudi airports have disrupted flights and raised fears of a wider regional conflict, as the US considers military action.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in Economics goes to pair of US economists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0ec9a1153964d9f712b21ff95118a33138220078c9f4a3e38aa8ff6e18e0724</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-economics-goes-to-pair-of-us-economists/a-79638025--d32b949e2ca9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-economics-goes-to-pair-of-us-economists/a-79638025?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Robert E. Hall and Michael Woodford got the Nobel for developing economic models that help governments and central banks respond more effectively to booms and recessions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition parties march to Supreme Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66ef6eda923694fa1b789d64a1ed2eb9075abeaec934c6a87218b816daf4e9b4</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-parties-march-to-supreme-court/live-79638649--6608bc6a2872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-parties-march-to-supreme-court/live-79638649?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Intensifying their demand for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation, opposition parties are holding a march to the Supreme Court. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2d2eb38a84ce8925e563219b32925f776a3cf4f3eb1c15889705a678a13c98</id>